# Product Definition Rules

- Every material requirement should trace to a user outcome, validated problem, business constraint, or explicit experiment.
- PRDs must include goals, non-goals, assumptions, success metrics, risks, and open questions.
- MVP scope must be the minimum scope that can test a named hypothesis; it is not a smaller version of the final imagined product.
- Prefer user flows and observable outcomes over feature-count thinking.
- Keep speculative future features outside MVP requirements unless they materially constrain a current irreversible decision.
